.TH LOLA 1
.SH NAME
lola \- window system
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lola
[
.BI "-i " cmd
]
[
.B -s
]
[
.B -t
]
[
.BI "-T " theme
]
[
.BI "-theme " theme
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Lola
is a window system based on the architecture of
.IR rio (1).
It manages text windows on a raster display and serves the usual
.B /dev
window interface mounted at
.BR /mnt/wsys .
.PP
The
.B -i
option runs
.I cmd
as an initialization command after startup.
This is normally a script containing
.IR window (1)
commands.
.PP
The
.B -s
option starts windows in scrolling mode.
The
.B -t
option enables experimental tabbed windows.
.PP
The
.B -T
and
.B -theme
options select the window decoration theme.
The available themes are
.BR flat ,
.BR simple ,
.BR win3 ,
and
.BR win95 .
If no theme is specified,
.B simple
is used.
.PP
.I Lola
supports the usual
.IR rio (1)
window controls and adds decorated windows, virtual desktops, window
picking via the
.B pick
file, and additional
.B wctl
messages including
.BR screenoffset ,
.BR sticky ,
.BR nosticky ,
.BR title ,
.BR notitle ,
.BR border ,
.BR noborder ,
and
.BR newtab .
.PP
Button 3 on the desktop opens the window menu.
A button 1-2 chord on the desktop opens the screen menu for virtual
desktops.
.SH FILES
.TF /mnt/wsys
.TP
.B /mnt/wsys
mounted window system file tree
.TP
.B /dev/wctl
window control file
.SH SOURCE
.B /sys/src/cmd/lola
